2026-09-01T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2144) 'The DR runbook runs for real, and the break-glass CA it needed lands in 1Password.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2144) 'RFD66606-2143 called its own DR runbook theatre because RFD66606-2141's break-glass CA was not in 1Password. On 2026-09-01, `weftspun-fdb`, `weftspun-bao`, `spot-broker` and `chibifire-com` were gone from Fly.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2144) 'Check that `fdbbackup describe` reports `Restorable: true` for the R2 bucket before you rely on the restore, then read below for the `fdbrestore` timings.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2144) 'The DR runbook runs, and the CA it needed lands
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2144) 'Mint the break-glass CA at DR-time, stash to `op://Personal/FDB-CA/`, execute the R2-primary restore, and land the follow-ups the run surfaces: Bao secret hygiene, R2 key rotation, Tigris fan-out refresh, scale to three at `double` redundancy. The CA in 1P closes RFD66606-2141's prereq; the runbook stops being theatre.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2144) 'RFD66606-2141's phases 2–3 rotate the machine leaves to certificates the restored Bao PKI mount signs, once Bao is unsealed against the restored FDB. Until then, the cluster runs on the break-glass CA.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2144  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2144) '`logbook-rfd2144-dr-runbook-first-run.md` records what was measured during the run itself.
 # tags: rfd:decision
